30,2,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Mio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,It seems that sitting close to one another really helps the team learn and collaborate more naturally than we might realize.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"I've found that the current plan creates an imbalance in window access, and past shuffles have caused significant disruptions to our work.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The costs are... quite high. Re-running the power is expensive per desk, and we're paying for floor area regardless of how many of us are actually sitting there.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Mio,,"It turns out that a ""free"" system isn't actually free in terms of time! Setting up every morning takes a few minutes, and people arrive at very different times.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The sound levels vary quite a bit across the room, and the physio's notes suggest that getting a workstation actually comfortable is a slow, tedious process.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Toshio, if the current plan is unfair regarding the windows, perhaps we should consider a system where no one is permanently stuck in a less desirable spot.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"That is a logical suggestion, Shizue. If we avoid permanent assignments, we eliminate the risk of some people being disadvantaged by the layout for the long term.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"But if we change things too often, the cost of re-running the power and network will just keep adding up... it might be too expensive.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mio,,"That's a good point, Daisuke! But we also have to think about the time we lose every morning if we're constantly moving. I don't want us to waste our energy just getting settled.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"Exactly. If it takes days to get a chair and monitor just right, moving every few weeks or every single morning sounds like a nightmare for my back.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"I understand. It sounds like we are balancing the need for collaboration and fairness against the costs of time, money, and physical comfort.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"If we prioritize stability to avoid the disruption of shuffles and the cost of rewiring, we must find a way to address the window inequality fairly.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I just worry that if we don't keep it simple, the budget will be gone before we even finish the move. Maybe we should avoid any plan that requires frequent changes.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Mio,,"I agree with Daisuke on the budget, but I'm still worried about the morning rush! If we go with fixed desks, we save time and money, but we're back to the window problem.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"If we go with fixed desks, we at least solve the ergonomics and noise issues. I can't be expected to fight with a monitor arm every single morning just to avoid a window dispute.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,It seems we are torn between the efficiency of fixed seats and the fairness of a flexible system. Perhaps there is a middle ground that allows for some change without being a daily burden?,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,A rotating system could potentially balance the window access issue without the daily chaos of a free-address layout or the permanence of fixed desks.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I'm not sure... wouldn't rotating still mean we have to pay for the network and power to be moved every time we shift?,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Mio,,"That's a really good question, Daisuke! I wonder if rotating blocks means we just move as a group to desks that are already wired, rather than moving the wires themselves?","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"If we're just swapping pre-wired blocks, it might be tolerable, but I'm still concerned about the time it takes to adjust the equipment to my liking.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
