58,3,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Since we've weighed the costs and the benefits of collaboration, I think we are ready to look at the options and decide what works best for everyone.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Given the data, we must choose between Free Address, Fixed Desks by Function, or Rotating Blocks. I believe Rotating Blocks is the most equitable way to handle the window disparity.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm still worried about the budget. If we can't avoid the rewiring costs, Fixed Desks by Function seems like the safest choice for the department's finances.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Mio,,"I'm torn! Fixed desks save time and money, but Rotating Blocks sounds like a fun way to keep things fair. I'll have to think about which one is less stressful for our daily flow.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"I'm leaning toward Fixed Desks. Between the noise levels and the physio's warning about equipment adjustment, I can't support any system that forces me to reset my workstation repeatedly.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"I see the value in both stability and fairness. However, knowing how much the new joiners benefited from overhearing us, I worry that Fixed Desks by Function might isolate us too much.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Shizue, that is a valid point, but Rotating Blocks would still allow for group interaction while ensuring that no one is permanently relegated to the interior wall.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"If we rotate, do we still have to pay for the network changes? I really can't support anything that keeps draining the budget.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Daisuke, I think we can just move our laptops and notebooks! If the desks are already there, we aren't moving the actual power outlets, right? That would save the budget and our time!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"Even if we just move our laptops, I still have to spend days tweaking the chair and monitor arm at every new spot. That's a productivity killer I can't ignore.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"I understand your frustration, Shunichi. However, if we choose Fixed Desks, we risk losing that spontaneous learning and connection that helps our new colleagues feel welcome and integrated.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"If we prioritize the social integration Shizue mentions and the fairness I seek, Rotating Blocks is the only option that addresses both without the daily inefficiency of Free Address.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I suppose if we aren't paying for new wiring every time we move, Rotating Blocks might be okay. I just want to make sure we aren't wasting money.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Mio,,"I'm totally for Rotating Blocks then! It's a great compromise—it's fair, it keeps us together, and it doesn't waste our mornings like Free Address would.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"I still find the physical toll of resetting my workstation unacceptable, but if the rest of you are this set on it, I can't realistically fight the majority.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Shizue,,It seems we have found a path that respects both our need for fairness and our budget. I will cast my vote for Rotating Blocks.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Toshio,,I agree that it is the most balanced solution for the team. I vote for Rotating Blocks.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I'll go with Rotating Blocks too... as long as we're careful with the costs.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Mio,,I'm all in! Rotating Blocks it is! I vote for Rotating Blocks!,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"I'll vote for Rotating Blocks as well, though I'm still not thrilled about the ergonomics.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
